{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the wrapper.</b> This term is known in the words of our early sages of blessed memory, and the meaning is like a cloak in which one wraps oneself." "<b>Fine linen.</b> It is linen, and it is a type of flax species in Egypt, and it is fine and precious." "<b>And the city of Shushan.</b> Where the Jews were."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:17.680178328Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}